{"Django querysets do not support negative slicing - queryset[start_offset:stop] with negative start_offset will cause runtime errors or undefined behavior": 0.9047266244888306, "OptimizedCursorPaginator violates the pattern of rejecting negative offsets with BadPaginationError that all other paginators in the file follow": 0.946223258972168, "When offset is negative, the comparison len(results) == offset + limit + extra will produce incorrect results, causing wrong boundary detection": 0.8668683767318726, "Comment in Cursor class is misleading - the Cursor class accepts negative offsets without validation, but they are rejected by all standard paginators except the new OptimizedCursorPaginator which causes errors": 0.5453547835350037, "User-controlled query parameter optimized_pagination enables dangerous negative offset behavior in OptimizedCursorPaginator, allowing attackers with global access to craft malicious cursor values with negative offsets to trigger Django queryset errors or access unintended data": 0.9474890828132629, "Misleading comment in BasePaginator - Django querysets don't handle negative offsets, and the code prevents them with max(0, offset), but the comment suggests negative offsets are allowed for high-traffic scenarios": 0.5428465008735657}